;; talk/closing.scm — positions written when closing the first pass.
;; The first eight are on the eight user and maintainer decisions with the most decisions depending on them,
;; directly or through others, counted through :depends across the whole spec on 2026-11-19
;; (boundary 85, consent 62, how-many 37, programs 31, silence 27, private-who 26, trader-who 26,
;; institution-angle 20). Each states the option this author would choose and the strongest reason
;; against it, in one sentence.
;; The p-closer-critic- positions record where this author disagrees with the critic's gap list.

(position 'p-closer-boundary :by "opus-closer" :on 'd-kernel-boundary :for 'same-answer-for-everyone
  :because (guess "I would choose the one-true-answer test, though the strongest reason against it is that almost every fact passes it, and in one pass it has already pulled leaving, money in and out, keys, the could-lose figure and the rule for held payments into the kernel, so it may grow the kernel into the single interface for everyone that the owner ruled out."))

(position 'p-closer-consent :by "opus-closer" :on 'd-kernel-consent :for 'by-effect-with-floor
  :because (guess "I would choose asking by effect with a floor, though the strongest reason against it is that sorting signatures by effect needs a runtime statement of each signature's effect (k-effect) that does not exist, and the floor is already untrue on a hub's server and for a hub's automatic credit, so the leaning rests on runtime work and two stated exceptions."))

(position 'p-closer-how-many :by "opus-closer" :on 'd-kernel-how-many :for 'four
  :because (guess "I would choose four faces, though the strongest reason against it is that the protocol only tells apart one signer from a board and a device from a server, so most of what separates the private face from the trader face is policy that one face could carry, while each extra face multiplies every launch flow's owning tests in both wallets."))

(position 'p-closer-programs :by "opus-closer" :on 'd-kernel-programs :for 'one-program-four-faces
  :because (guess "I would choose one program with four faces, though the strongest reason against it is that this is the largest single piece of work in the design, it must be built in both wallets, and the rule that an entity is open in one face at a time is kept only by the program itself, which is the place faces would start to leak into each other."))

(position 'p-closer-silence :by "opus-closer" :on 'd-kernel-silence :for 'fact-and-sums
  :because (guess "I would choose a shared fact with each face's own response, though the strongest reason against it is that the trader face could only make its response bind its own programs by asking for a new kind of standing rule (d-kernel-silence-rule), which suggests that stopping new risk on silence may belong below the faces after all."))

(position 'p-closer-angle :by "opus-closer" :on 'd-institution-angle :for 'surface-not-angle
  :because (guess "I would choose to keep the institution face as a face and not as the rejected sales angle, though the strongest reason against it is that, without two runtime changes nobody has scheduled (a board appointing the watching service, and the runtime keeping the board's record), it ships with every account 'not covered' and with no audit flow, and its remaining features are the ones the rejected treasury pitch sold."))

(position 'p-closer-private-who :by "opus-closer" :on 'd-private-who :for 'holder
  :because (guess "I would build the private face first for someone who already holds digital dollars at their own address, though the strongest reason against it is that the newcomer, paid by someone already inside, is how the network grows, and a face built for holders assumes at joining an address and tokens the newcomer does not have."))

(position 'p-closer-trader-who :by "opus-closer" :on 'd-trader-who :for 'own-book
  :because (guess "I would build the trader face for one person trading money only they sign for, though the strongest reason against it is that much professional trading is done by desks and by programs, and if most of the first traders trade a desk's money or only watch a program, the first screen and the ticket are wrong for them and the desk case falls to the institution face, which cannot trade at speed."))

;; Where this author disagrees with the critic.

(position 'p-closer-critic-held-pay :by "opus-closer" :on 'd-kernel-held-pay-not-allowed :for 'direct-only
  :because (canon 'htlc-constants-are-simnet "The critic read the three faces as answering one question three ways. They answer two rules: the trader's refusal of real money follows no-real-funds-before-dispute-fix, which refuses real money on a chain altogether, and the private and institution payment rules follow this rule about held payments on an EVM mainnet, which they already answered alike. The kernel decision is still useful, because the shared answer had no owner, but there was no contradiction to resolve."))

(position 'p-closer-critic-reach :by "opus-closer" :on 'd-kernel-reach-channel :for 'every-device-of-the-entity
  :because (protocol "core/watchtower/push/store.ts" "The critic said the only grounded way to reach a person is a push to one phone. The service already keeps several device registrations per entity and wakes all of them, and it accepts a registration from any runtime that signs it, so a second device, each board member and the operator can each be woken today. What was missing was a decision that a face offers this, not a capability."))

(position 'p-closer-critic-unbuilt :by "opus-closer" :on 'd-kernel-unbuilt :for 'not-offered-until-built
  :because (guess "The critic is right that the checker counts a need as met when a guessed capability names it. The vocabulary cannot be changed here, so the fix is a convention and a decision: a capability resting on (protocol …) exists at its path, anything else is work not yet done and names d-kernel-unbuilt. A reader can now tell the two apart, but the checker still cannot, and a future check that counts needs met only by guesses would make this visible without reading every sentence."))
